<p style="text-align: center;"><img src="/images/2014/Meadow-Grove.jpg" alt="This landscape was created using a limited palette. It features hay bales, a middle-ground treeline and the Blue Ridge mountains in the far distance." width="450" height="338" /></p>
<p style="text-align: center;">Meadow Grove. 11" x 14" oil on linen panel. 2014</p>
<p style="text-align: left;">I'm gearing up for the first of my summer shows: &nbsp;Upperville Stable Tour, over Memorial Day weekend and the Western Loudoun Artist Studio Tour the third weekend in June.</p>
<p style="text-align: left;">This latest painting is a landscape that I've been contemplating for a couple of years, but I steered away from because of the amount of green in the picture. &nbsp;By using a simple palette of chromatic black, burnt sienna and lemon yellow I managed to find a nice solution to the green problem and convey the feel of the meadow in the summer heat.</p>
<p style="text-align: left;">I'll have this for sale at Upperville on the 23rd and 24th May.</p>
